{"type":"message","id":"929b84d1","parentId":"fa51b9c9","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:07:37.772Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9f6b09551cc21b68","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"mode\": \"deep_research\",\n  \"story_id\": \"how-a-crypto-exchange-secretly-hid-53m-in-stolen-crypto-to-prevent-a-bank-run-as\",\n  \"category\": \"sec-vs-cryptocurrency\",\n  \"wp_category_slugs\": [\n    \"sec-vs-cryptocurrency\"\n  ],\n  \"wp_category_ids\": [\n    192\n  ],\n  \"topic_theme\": \"How a crypto exchange secretly hid $53M in stolen crypto to prevent a bank run – as the SEC  targets its directors\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"How a crypto\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"How a crypto exchange secretly hid $53M in stolen crypto to prevent a bank run – as the SEC  targets its directors\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Bitcoin\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"bitcoin\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"cryptoslate.com\",\n    \"bitcoinfoundation.org\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cryptoslate.com/how-a-crypto-exchange-secretly-hid-53m-in-stolen-crypto-to-prevent-a-bank-run-and-why-the-sec-is-finally-coming-for-its-directors/\",\n    \"https://bitcoinfoundation.org/news/crypto-companies-news/thai-sec-accuses-bitkub-of-concealing-51-million-hack/\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Thailand's Securities and Exchange Commission has filed a criminal complaint against Bitkub Online and two former directors, alleging that the crypto exchange submitted daily net-capital reports, known as Form DA 1, that failed to show the effect of a 2021 theft involving about 1.7 billion baht (roughly $53 million) in customer assets.\",\n    \"A $50M exchange heist, a secret founder bailout, and a 5-month cover-up to prevent a bank run have finally caught up with Bitkub.\",\n    \"Crime Bearish One crypto wallet tied to a 20-year-old fraudster processed over $122M before Interpol closed in The Thailand case shows how cross-chain token swaps can complicate tracing across services, assets and borders.\",\n    \"The regulator said hackers stole crypto worth about 1.7 billion baht (or approximately $51 million) from Bitkub in May 2021.\",\n    \"He was previously a reporter at The Defiant, crypto.news, currency.com, iHodl, BeInCrypto, and other…\\n\\nThe nearly $300M DeFi exploit is turning into a blame fight, with LayerZero flagging risks and...\",\n    \"The controversial crypto project WLFI▼$0.0570, directly tied to President Donald Trump’s...\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"A $50M exchange heist, a secret founder bailout, and a 5-month cover-up to prevent a bank run have finally caught up with Bitkub.\\n\\nJul. 28, 2026 at 11:30 am GMT• 2 min read\\n\\n1. 01 Thai SEC alleges Bitkub concealed a 1.7 billion-baht 2021 theft in daily capital reports.\\n2. 02 Bitkub says nondisclosure prevented a bank run while co-founders replaced the stolen assets.\\n3. 03 Police will investigate before prosecutors decide whether to bring the still-unadjudicated case.\\n\\nThailand's Securities and Exchange Commission has filed a criminal complaint against Bitkub Online and two former directors, alleging that the crypto exchange submitted daily net-capital reports, known as Form DA 1, that failed to show the effect of a 2021 theft involving about 1.7 billion baht (roughly $53 million) in customer assets.\\n\\nThe July 23, 2026, complaint to Thailand's Economic Crime Suppression Division names Sakolkorn Sakavee and Thaweesap Rawan, who the SEC said were responsible for the reports when they were Bitkub directors. The regulator alleges that Bitkub gave false statements and that the two former directors made false entries in company documents.\\n\\nRelated Reading Dutch crypto exchange collapses exposing customer balances' true value amid multi-million-euro hole The court found an undisclosed deficit and said Knaken cannot repay customers in full, leaving recovery to an independent trustee. Jul 17, 2026·Liam 'Akiba' Wright\\n\\nAccording to the SEC, a May 2021 cyberattack caused customer assets across 16 cryptocurrencies to be withdrawn from the exchange. Bitkub's Form DA 1 reports from May 10 through Oct. 30, 2021, showed no material change in its asset balance from the theft, conduct the regulator said amounted to false reporting.\\n\\nThe SEC said subsequent information indicated that Bitkub began procuring replacement digital assets on Oct. 31, 2021. The regulator did not say when that replacement process was completed.\\n\\nRelated Reading The trick big crypto exchanges are using to mitigate hacks, yet can still lock up your money Exchanges can reimburse hacked balances, but they can’t stop the instant shock to liquidity and market depth. Dec 1, 2025·Gino Matos\\n\\nIn its response to the complaint, Bitkub acknowledged that personnel responsible for company disclosures chose not to reveal that assets from one company wallet had been stolen. The company said the decision was intended to prevent a bank run while Bitkub was trying to replace the assets. It disputed that the accused individuals had acted fraudulently.\\n\\nRelated Reading Crypto hacks hit a record count but the biggest threat isn’t smart contracts The industry's security problem is changing shape: more hacks, lower typical losses, and a handful of infrastructure compromises still defining the first half's damage. Jul 5, 2026·Liam 'Akiba' Wright\\n\\nBitkub said its co-founders absorbed the loss by buying the same currencies in the same quantities. It claimed that neither the company nor its customers suffered asset losses from the incident.\\n\\nCryptoSlate Daily Brief\\n Daily signals, zero noise.\\n\\nMarket-moving headlines and context delivered every morning in one tight read.\\n\\nFree. No spam. Unsubscribe any time.\\n\\nWhoops, looks like there was a problem. Please try again.\\n\\nIn a separate September 2025 update, the SEC said customer digital assets held by Bitkub were safe and complete as of Sept. 8, 2025. That finding covered a later point in time and did not settle the regulator's allegation about what Bitkub reported in 2021.\\n\\nAsset replacement and regulatory reporting remain separate questions in the complaint. Bitkub says the nondisclosure was intended to avert a bank run; the SEC alleges that the daily reports failed to show a material change in the exchange's assets before replacement began.\\n\\nAn inquiry official will now investigate and decide whether to recommend prosecution, according to the SEC's criminal-action process. A public prosecutor would then consider the file, and a court would adjudicate the allegations only if the case is brought. The allegations remain unadjudicated.\\n\\nAlso known as \\\"Akiba,\\\" Liam Wright is a reporter, podcast producer, and Editor-in-Chief at CryptoSlate. He believes that decentralized technology has the potential to make widespread positive change.\\n\\nExplore related reporting by asset, place, or topic.\\n\\nCrime Bearish One crypto wallet tied to a 20-year-old fraudster processed over $122M before Interpol closed in The Thailand case shows how cross-chain token swaps can complicate tracing across services, assets and borders. 2 weeks ago\\n\\nAnalysis These three Asian markets got the jump on tokenized finance over the US $30 billion on Japanese exchanges edges toward BTC as custody rules harden. 9 months ago\\n\\nPeople Thailand’s DV8 Bitcoin treasury push deepens as Jason Fang becomes CEO after 99.9% raise Sora’s MicroStrategy 2.0 strategy now lands in Thailand, raising stakes for an ASEAN hub. 11 months ago\\n\\nDeFi SEC warning over crypto yield vaults puts DeFi’s secret human controllers in the crosshairs Why your crypto yield vault might actually be an illegal fund under SEC scrutiny. 22 hours ago\\n\\nRegulation Lawsuit claims 3.8M dormant BTC using police lost-and-found rules as Congress races to stop it with CLARITY New CLARITY language would shield dormant self-custodied Bitcoin from state lost-property claims based on inactivity alone. 2 days ago\\n\\nAI Usage Disclosure\\nCryptoSlate may use AI tools to support research, editing, and production workflows. Published articles remain editorially reviewed by our team. Read our full AI usage disclaimer.\\n\\nDisclaimer\\nOur writers' opinions are solely their own and do not reflect the opinion of CryptoSlate. None of the information you read on CryptoSlate should be taken as investment advice, nor does CryptoSlate endorse any project that may be mentioned or linked to in this article. Buying and trading cryptocurrencies should be considered a high-risk activity. Please do your own due diligence before taking any action related to content within this article. Finally, CryptoSlate takes no responsibility should you lose money trading cryptocurrencies. For more information, see our company disclaimers.\\n\\nLatest Guide What is Dogecoin?Learn what Dogecoin is, how DOGE mining works, why supply keeps growing, and how to weigh payment use...1 month ago7.6 Crypto Cards Review Kast Card KAST turns a stablecoin balance into a spendable USD Visa that works in 170+ countries, including the US...1 hour ago7.5 Project Report G Coin: Playnance’s On-Chain Entertainment Economy An independent analysis of G Coin, covering its role in Playnance’s on-chain entertainment ecosystem, token utility, tokenomics, audits,...3 months ago\\n\\nCryptoSlate Newsletter \\n Daily signals. Zero noise.\\n\\nGet market-moving headlines, on-chain insights, and editor picks delivered in one tight read.\\n\\nEmail address \\nWe respect your privacy and will never share your email address.\\n\\nDaily signals, editor picks, and market context are on the way.\\n\\nYou may unsubscribe at any time.\\n\\nDisclaimer: By using this website, you agree to our Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy. CryptoSlate has no affiliation or relationship with any company or project unless explicitly stated otherwise. CryptoSlate is an informational website that provides news about coins, companies and products. None of the information you read on CryptoSlate should be taken as investment advice. Buying and trading cryptocurrencies should be considered a high-risk activity. Please do your own diligence before making any investment decisions. CryptoSlate is not accountable, directly or indirectly, for any damage or loss incurred, alleged or otherwise, in connection to the use of or reliance on any content you read on the site. Read all disclaimers\\n\\n---\\n\\nThai SEC says Bitkub concealed a 2021 theft for nearly six months, while the exchange says the decision was intended to prevent a bank run.\\n\\nThailand’s Securities and Exchange Commission has filed a criminal complaint against Bitkub, the country’s largest crypto exchange, and two former directors over reports submitted after a previously undisclosed 2021 hack.\\n\\nThe regulator said hackers stole crypto worth about 1.7 billion baht (or approximately $51 million) from Bitkub in May 2021. Still, daily filings submitted between May 10 and October 30 showed no material change in the company’s assets, according to the SEC. The regulator said:\\n\\n“The SEC further found that Bitkub did not report to the SEC in its daily net capital report (Form DA 1) in a manner consistent with the theft incident.”\\n\\nForm DA 1 reports are used by the regulator to track an exchange’s financial position. The SEC alleged that Bitkub’s reports therefore contained false information and gave the impression that customer assets were being held normally and that the company had suffered no damage.\\n\\nSakolkorn Sakavee and Thaweesap Rawan, Bitkub’s directors at the time, were responsible for submitting the reports and were named alongside the company in the complaint.\\n\\nBitkub acknowledged in a statement that people responsible for its disclosures had “decided not to disclose” that one of the company’s wallets had been stolen. It said the decision was intended “to prevent a bank run.” The exchange added:\\n\\n“Had a bank run occurred, customers could have suffered widespread losses, and Thailand’s digital-asset industry could also have been harmed.”\\n\\nBitkub also said the incident “did not result from fraudulent conduct” by those named in the complaint. The crypto exchange added that its co-founders later absorbed the loss by buying the same cryptocurrencies in the same amounts, although the stolen assets were never recovered.\\n\\nCrypto news reporter at Bitcoin Foundation covering topics including crypto markets, DeFi exploits, and regulatory developments. He was previously a reporter at The Defiant, crypto.news, currency.com, iHodl, BeInCrypto, and other…\\n\\nThe nearly $300M DeFi exploit is turning into a blame fight, with LayerZero flagging risks and...\\n\\nThe controversial crypto project WLFI▼$0.0570, directly tied to President Donald Trump’s...\\n\\nGemini shares jumped after Tyler and Cameron Winklevoss invested $100 million in the struggling...\\n\\nBinance MiCA license push will continue in another EU country after its Greece application...\\n\\nA Ledger security team says Tangem Bitcoin wallet cards can be broken with a laser attack that lets...\\n\\nThe company believes crypto industry security is a shared responsibility. Ripple is providing its...\\n\\nBitcoin Price Prediction 2026: Will BTC Finally Rally to 100k?Bitcoin was the first to introduce cryptocurrency. It…\\n Ethereum Price Prediction 2026. Will ETH Reach New All-Time Highs in 2026?Ethereum is currently the foundation for the smart…\\n Top 5 Crazy Bitcoin Price Predictions 2026: Will BTC Hit $1M?A number of people who predict prices for…\\n XRP Price Prediction 2026: Is a Major Drop Coming for Ripple?The XRP▲$1.13 price prediction 2026 has become one…\\n Bittensor Price Prediction: What Analysts Expect from Leading AI TAO Crypto Among coins tied to AI, few draw as…\\n\\nYour trusted source for cryptocurrency news, market analysis, and blockchain insights.\\n\\n© 2026 Bitcoin Foundation. All rights reserved.\",\n  \"partial_words\": 1720\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1785240457772}}
